The marquise has the most raw face-up per carat of any shape — its points extend further than any rectangular or oval outline. The elongated emerald cut exceeds the oval in face-up area and surpasses the round brilliant by a meaningful margin. The step-cut format means every millimeter of that face-up area is a clean, open mirror surface — not a collection of tiny brilliant facets.

That surface reads as one unbroken expanse of reflected light. Visually, it presents as larger than its face-up dimensions suggest.

