The price reflects rarity — finding a 3ct+ rough that yields an elongated step-cut above VS1 clarity is genuinely difficult.

> "The elongated emerald cut is the most honest shape in the market. The step facets don't hide anything — not inclusions below VS1 and not the actual size of the stone. What you see in the photograph is what you get on the hand. That transparency cuts both ways: it rewards buyers who understand the clarity rules and punishes buyers who skip them." — Farzana Hasan, **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**

